{
  "borough": "Harrow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height:normal&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt&quot;&gt;The proposed rear dormer and roof extension, by reason of its excessive size and bulk, would result in an overly dominant form of development that would be unduly obtrusive and incongruous and would detract from the appearance of the subject property and adjacent properties, to the detriment of the character and appearance of the subject property and the surrounding area, contrary to the high quality design aspirations of the National Planning Policy Framework (2023, Policy D3.D.1 and D.11 of The London Plan (2021), Policy CS1.B of the Harrow Core Strategy (2012), Policy DM1 of the Development Management Plan Local Policies (2013) and the adopted Supplementary Planning Document: Residential Design Guide (2010).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height:normal&quot;&gt;The proposal, by reason of insufficient head height for the second floor flat, would provide an overall cramped and substandard quality of living accommodation, to the detriment of the residential amenities of the existing and future occupiers of the unit, contrary to policies DM1 and DM 26 of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;ol start=&quot;2&quot;&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height:normal&quot;&gt;The proposal, by reason of failure to demonstrate sufficient internal floor&amp;nbsp;space,&amp;nbsp; fails to demonstrate that the first and second floor units would provide an overall acceptable standard of living accommodation. The proposed development would therefore give rise to substandard and poor quality accommodation to the detriment of the residential amenities of existing and future occupiers of the units, contrary to policies DM26 (c) of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013), The London Planning Guidance - Housing Design Guide (June 2023)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br data-cke-eol=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
